WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.961
[MUSIC]

00:00:00.961 --> 00:00:04.628
You're so busy running and
competing for meetings and

00:00:04.628 --> 00:00:09.332
time that the ability to stop and
pause and recharge your batteries and

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:14.710
think broader and much deeper was
really a terrific opportunity.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:18.660
What I took from SCP and
what I think I'm doing differently is

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.710
consciously thinking about not
only what I need to do today, but

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.490
how that bridge is to where business
goes in the future as well.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.620
One of the highlights of
coming to Stanford was it is

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.820
right in the middle of
the technology corridor.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.630
To be right in the heart of The Silicon
Valley, I think, is a huge benefit.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:41.020
To think differently to,
how to be more open to the ideas and

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:46.030
concepts and to really define how we serve
customers in a differentiated way is

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:48.980
really a great part of being right here.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.450
SEP, I consider it an incredible
investment in me as a lead.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:55.260
Think about the incredible
investment my family made.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.380
Because in the middle of summer
your kids are out of school.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.750
How do I balance all that?

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.950
And I would say, make the time,
because you have so

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.390
much more to give back to others.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:09.270
One of the really key benefits of
the program is building a global network

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.610
that enables you to think differently,

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.180
not only about what we do here in
the U.S., but around the world as well.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.800
Coaching and developing and
sending talent to programs such as SEP

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.540
really enables companies to maintain
relevancy, maintain a competitive edge,

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:26.020
and maintain a leadership position.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.860
Don't be the person who has all
the answers but rather be the leader who

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:36.190
facilitates different kind of conversation
as a result of what you've learned.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:41.730
Our credo, which is what we live by,
says our best was good for

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.780
today, tomorrow we will do better.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:49.540
The investment Verizon made for me to
attend SEP has made me a better leader,

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.159
and in return I believe I make
the business better every day.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.970
I really believe that SEP was
transformational, because it gave me

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:01.030
a platform on which to think about
the business differently, and in thinking

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.330
about the business differently, to deliver
different kind of performance results.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:07.572
It will be the best
investment you've ever made.

00:02:07.572 --> 00:02:09.051
[SOUND]

